   "Overall top width 7'-10\"/8'-1\"/8'-10\" (48/54/72) = 56 + 2*(H-8)/4 + 18; each top flange 1'-4\" wide.",
   "Inner face: 3\" x 3\" chamfer off the 10\" bottom slab, then a 1:4 face up to 21\" below the top (4'-3 1/8\" apart at the chamfer top), then 1 15/16\" further out over the top 21\" to the flange inner edge; the lower segment is 1'-2\", 1'-8\" and 3'-2\" high for FUB-48/54/72 (H - 34).",
   "Outer face 1:4 from the 4'-8\" soffit to 8\" below the top, flange underside rising 1\" over 8 1/2\" to the edge, 1/2\" edge draft over 7\", 3/4\" chamfer at the bottom of the top-flange edge and 1 1/2\" soffit chamfers.",
   "Residuals: area -0.01 to -0.07 %, Ixx +0.03 to +0.06 %, Iyy +0.05 to +0.14 % (Iyy for FUB-54+ printed to 4 significant figures), yb +0.01 to +0.10 %. PCI Journal 2021 lists slightly larger areas (1207.5 for FUB-48), so FDOT's own table is the reference here."
